// TESTVEC - test several candidate vectors against [A] at once (for MCQ options).
// [A] = the matrix, [B] = the candidate vectors as columns.
// If the vectors have as many entries as [A] has columns: shows A*v, whether A*v = 0
// (v in Null(A)) and, for square [A], whether v is an eigenvector and its eigenvalue.
// If they have as many entries as [A] has rows: whether v is in Col(A).
// Out: B = rank(A) (when tested against Col(A)), [E] = A*v for the last vector
ClrHome
Disp "TEST VECTORS","A = [A]","VECTORS = COLS OF [B]"
dim([A])→ʟZD
ʟZD(1)→G
ʟZD(2)→H
dim([B])→ʟZD
ʟZD(1)→U
ʟZD(2)→V
If U≠H and U≠G:Then
Disp "ROWS OF [B] MUST EQUAL","ROWS OR COLS OF [A]"
Return
End
// rank of A, to compare with rank [A|v] for the column space test
If U=G:Then
[A]→[J]
0→S
0→Q
0→W
prgmZRREF
R→B
End
For(L,1,V)
Matr►list([B],L,ʟTV)
max(abs(ʟTV))→E
ClrHome
Disp "VECTOR",L
If U=H:Then
List►matr(ʟTV,[C])
[A]*[C]→[E]
Matr►list([E],1,ʟTW)
max(abs(ʟTW))→Z
Disp "A*V ="
Pause [E]►Frac
If Z≤1ᴇ⁻9*max(1,E):Then
Disp "A*V=0: IN NULL(A)"
If G=H and E>1ᴇ⁻12
Disp "EIGENVECTOR, LAMBDA=0"
Else
If G=H:Then
// lambda from the first non-zero entry of v, then check A*v = lambda*v
1→D
While abs(ʟTV(D))≤1ᴇ⁻12
D+1→D
End
ʟTW(D)/ʟTV(D)→O
If max(abs(ʟTW-O*ʟTV))≤1ᴇ⁻9*max(1,Z):Then
Disp "EIGENVECTOR, LAMBDA="
Disp O►Frac
Else
Disp "NOT AN EIGENVECTOR"
End
End
End
End
If U=G:Then
List►matr(ʟTV,[D])
augment([A],[D])→[J]
0→S
0→Q
0→W
prgmZRREF
If R=B:Then
Disp "IN COL(A)"
Else
Disp "NOT IN COL(A)"
End
End
If E≤1ᴇ⁻12
Disp "(ZERO VECTOR)"
Pause
End
